    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 score makes him our premier play as he faces Painter (xERA 4.67). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% boost from both a favorable park and pitcher skill gap, further amplified by his presence in the #3 hole. Providing strong support at the top of the order, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.23) and **Sam Antonacci** (65.85) are our most efficient speed threats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** exploits a 14% platoon edge against Elder, while **Sam Antonacci** utilizes his lead-off spot to maximize plate appearances against Martinez. We are also projecting a high ceiling for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.83), whose raw power remains stable despite the slight penalty from a dynamic platoon disadvantage.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Coby Mayo** (58.32) in the UTIL slot over **Jorge Polanco** (50.55). While **Coby Mayo** faces a tough pitcher-catcher dynamic, the park factors and higher base projection pushed him over the edge. **Jorge Polanco** remains our most viable bench depth, though he was excluded today primarily due to a lower projected efficiency and a sub-optimal spot in the bottom third of the batting order. We are keeping a close watch on **Jacob Wilson**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; their lineups remain pending, and we are relying on historical positional data to justify their inclusion. **Andy Pages** is of particular interest as he draws a start against a tough Ranger Suarez, with his moderate score elevated by his potential for stolen bases against a pitcher with a slow delivery. \n\nBe advised that today\u2019s slate carries distinct volatility: **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** face the formidable Ranger Suarez, whose xERA of 3.48 significantly dampens our base expectations. While we continue to navigate the absence of **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, the depth provided by **Denzer Guzman** and others on the bench remains ready to pivot should weather or late-scratched lineups disrupt our current configuration.",
